WEBVTT


00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:06.520
You know, one of the most common things going on right now is foreclosure repos.

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:09.860
Uh, most of my clients are facing custody battles

00:00:09.861 --> 00:00:11.960
or something going on with their kids.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:19.380
And my first step when I teach into all of my mentees that learn under me

00:00:19.381 --> 00:00:25.000
is to always get a trust. Get a trust.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.140
Get a trust. Get a trust.

00:00:27.141 --> 00:00:30.960
I cannot stress it enough to have a trust.

00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:32.580
If you don't have a trust,

00:00:32.581 --> 00:00:37.280
the state owns your kids. That house you don't truly own yet.

00:00:37.380 --> 00:00:38.580
You really don't truly own it

00:00:38.581 --> 00:00:41.980
because people don't even understand that you're just a tenant of occupancy.

00:00:41.981 --> 00:00:43.580
Even when you signed on a house,

00:00:43.581 --> 00:00:44.940
they don't care about a mortgage.

00:00:44.941 --> 00:00:46.400
They don't care about that payment.

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.940
You're just a tenant. And when they wanna go for clothes on it and take it back,

00:00:50.941 --> 00:00:53.220
they can because you did not protect your house.

00:00:53.221 --> 00:00:54.660
You did not accept the deed.

00:00:54.661 --> 00:00:56.280
You did not convey the property.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.820
Your house is unprotected.

00:00:57.821 --> 00:01:00.660
Your kids is unprotected. Your cars are unprotected.

00:01:00.661 --> 00:01:04.180
So that repo can happen at any given moment.

00:01:04.181 --> 00:01:07.200
But when you get a trust and you protect your assets,

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:09.300
who's stopping you? Who's,

00:01:09.301 --> 00:01:13.520
who's checking for you? Who's checking for you? Get a trust.
